---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { url } from "../paths";
import desktop from "../assets/shell/desktop.jpg";
import launcher from "../assets/shell/launcher.jpg";
import commands from "../assets/shell/commands.jpg";
import commandsNotes from "../assets/shell/commands-notes.jpg";
import commandsFtp from "../assets/shell/commands-ftp.jpg";
import notesMenu from "../assets/shell/notes-menu.jpg";
import ftpMenu from "../assets/shell/ftp-menu.jpg";
import quickSettings from "../assets/shell/quick-settings.jpg";
import settingsAppearance from "../assets/shell/settings-appearance.jpg";
import settingsPanels from "../assets/shell/settings-panels.jpg";
import settingsPlugins from "../assets/shell/settings-plugins.jpg";
import settingsLauncher from "../assets/shell/settings-launcher.jpg";
import settingsWidgets from "../assets/shell/settings-widgets.jpg";

const wide = [720, 1100, 1440, 1920];
const half = [640, 960, 1280, 1600];
---

<div class="shell-page">
  <section class="band shell-intro">
    <h1>
      <img src={url("rivet-shell.svg")} width="72" height="72" alt="" />
      Rivet Shell
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A Wayland desktop: a panel, a dock, widgets, and the wallpaper. There is no release yet, so you
      build it from source. Rough edges are expected.
    </p>
    <p>
      How to build it, and the commands, are in the <a href={url("docs/shell/")}>shell docs</a>.
    </p>
    <figure class="shell-shot">
      <Image
        src={desktop}
        alt="Rivet Shell with a floating top panel, a clock and system readings, and a dock, over a sunset wallpaper"
        widths={wide}
        sizes="(min-width: 800px) 72vw, 100vw"
      />
      <figcaption>The desktop. The panel floats at the top.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="band shell-settings" aria-labelledby="shell-settings">
    <h2 id="shell-settings">Settings</h2>
    <p>
      The settings window has pages for Wallpaper, Appearance, Panels, Dock, Widgets, Launcher,
      Notifications, Displays, Idle &amp; Lock, Plugins, and About.
    </p>
    <div class="shell-grid">
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={settingsAppearance} alt="Rivet Shell settings, Appearance page, with style, accent, and color use" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>Appearance.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={settingsPanels} alt="Rivet Shell settings, Panels page, with a floating top panel and its items" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>Panels.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={settingsWidgets} alt="Rivet Shell settings, Widgets page, with the clock and system readings" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>Widgets. A clock, and processor, memory, and battery.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={settingsLauncher} alt="Rivet Shell settings, Launcher page, with grid layout and size" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>Launcher.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={settingsPlugins} alt="Rivet Shell settings, Plugins page, with the official Notes and FTP plugins" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>Plugins. Notes and FTP are official plugins.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band shell-panel" aria-labelledby="shell-panel">
    <h2 id="shell-panel">Panel</h2>
    <p>
      The panel can float at the top. You choose the items: launcher, workspaces, window title,
      clock, media, system, volume, brightness, network, Bluetooth, battery, dock, tray,
      notifications, quick settings, and power. A plugin can add its own item.
    </p>
    <figure class="shell-shot">
      <Image
        src={quickSettings}
        alt="Rivet Shell quick settings: volume, brightness, toggles, and what is playing"
        widths={wide}
        sizes="(min-width: 800px) 72vw, 100vw"
      />
      <figcaption>Quick settings, opened from the panel.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="band shell-notes" aria-labelledby="shell-notes">
    <h2 id="shell-notes">Notes</h2>
    <p>
      Rivet Notes has an official shell plugin. Its panel item lists tasks and the latest notes, and
      a badge when a task is due. Choosing one opens Notes. It is a panel item, not a desktop widget.
      The launcher can start a new note, and <code>@notes</code> finds one by name.
    </p>
    <div class="shell-grid">
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={notesMenu} alt="The Notes panel item: tasks with a due badge, and the latest notes" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>The Notes item on the panel.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={commandsNotes} alt="The launcher after @notes, listing notes and New Note" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>@notes in the launcher, including New Note.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band shell-ftp" aria-labelledby="shell-ftp">
    <h2 id="shell-ftp">FTP</h2>
    <p>
      The FTP plugin puts saved connections on the panel, in groups. Choosing one opens Rivet FTP
      already connected to that server. It is a panel item, not a desktop widget.
      <code>@ftp</code> finds a connection in the launcher.
    </p>
    <div class="shell-grid">
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={ftpMenu} alt="The FTP panel item listing saved connections in groups" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>Saved connections on the panel.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={commandsFtp} alt="The launcher after @ftp, listing saved SFTP connections" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>@ftp in the launcher.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band shell-launch" aria-labelledby="shell-launch">
    <h2 id="shell-launch">Launcher</h2>
    <p>
      The launcher opens in the middle of the screen. <code>@</code> runs a command, such as
      <code>@notes</code> or <code>@ftp</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="shell-grid">
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={launcher} alt="The Rivet Shell launcher with app icons and an empty search field" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>The launcher.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shell-shot">
        <Image src={commands} alt="The launcher search starting with @ and offering Notes" widths={half} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 42vw, 100vw" />
        <figcaption>Typing @.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p>A panel item for Rivet Edit is coming soon.</p>
  </section>
</div>
